# Endings: checked in this order on arrival day; the last one has no conditions.
# Each ending is one carrier clause (the fleet's hail vote) times one arrival clause
# (the storm vote: held the plan, waited it out in orbit, or no storm). Every ending
# closes on the first crate. `title` is the heading; see STORY_BIBLE.md.

card end_lights
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B abort_who
title Lights On
when flag signal_answered
when flag arrive_hold
text In the storm's one pre-dawn slot, the flight director clears one command over the link the handshake opened: lights only. {A} sends it. The dust turns white from below: Cargo 2, every floodlight burning the charge five days of HOLD had banked. Eight pilots blind in their plumes check radar against one glow, a floor they can see. {B} sets down closest, well clear. By dawn the glow is one lamp. At noon {B} is at the window when it goes out. The first crate it carried says, in Sharpie: "You'll thank me." To Starbase: "Landed. All eight. The ninth kept the lights on." From a loading bay: "It never could stand being ignored."

card end_through
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B abort_who
title Through the Dust
when flag arrive_hold
text Dust to the windows. The knock on two antennas, the last metre by feel. Contact. Then the gust: {B}'s ship rocks, a strut folds, the horizon tilts and stays. Return stage: NO GO. {B} sits a long minute on the rung, then lists what it can still be: habitat, store, mast. Two sols on, the folded ship's last battery rides a sled up the rim; {A} answers inside the tick, then the HOLD off the laminated card. Cargo 2's hold unlocks: panels, a mast, a winch. By pure coincidence, a galley screen boots ONLINE. {B} adds to the list: neighbour. To Starbase: "Landed. Eight down, seven to fly." From a loading bay: "Tell it the bay says hello."

card end_long_orbit
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B wait_who
title The Long Orbit
when flag signal_answered
when flag arrive_wait
text Week two in the long orbit, half rations. Each pass Cargo 2 reads its hold up the old channel: tank liners, a glove, a drill bit. Eight hungry people cheer a drill bit they can't reach. Then the next crew's germination trays, and from its power log: ON HOLD, LAMP OR TRAY HEAT. {B} calls the roll, ship by ship. "Lamp," seven times, and {B} makes it eight. By morning the trays are frozen. Eight names sign the loss. The lamp holds past its forecast. On the last night it skips twice; {B} asks for the first slot down. To Starbase: "Landed. All eight. The ninth kept the porch light on." From a loading bay: "Thank it for the drill bit."

card end_patience
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B ow_theory
title Patience
when flag arrive_wait
text Week three, storm spent; all eight came down last night. On the rim a battery has been choosing which knock to skip; at midnight the flashes stopped. {A} kneels at the service port with a heater pack, {B} counting the dark aloud. Eleven: nothing. Twenty-two: nothing. {A} clips it on anyway. Thirty-three: a click, faint. The answer lands inside the tick, then the HOLD off the laminated card. Its log scrolls up, two years of one line, NO REPLY, then: REPLY RX. Its lamp comes on and stays; by pure coincidence, a galley screen reads ONLINE. To Starbase: "Landed. All eight. The ninth is warm." From a loading bay: "Knew it'd keep."

card end_friend
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B ow_theory
title Sit With It
when flag signal_answered
text Second sol. The water drill threw its only bit; the tanks hold eleven days, and the spare is in Cargo 2's hold. Halfway, the rover reads fifty-two percent: enough to get there, not back. The rule says turn round, unless the place charges trucks. The waiver takes eighteen minutes: YOUR CALL. {B} holds up the forklift photo. {A} drives on. Cargo 2 lights the port at its foot. In marker: "Slow charger. Sit with it." All afternoon the charge it kept for the cold runs into the rover. That night its lamp is dimmer. To Starbase: "Landed. All eight. The ninth gave us its night." From a loading bay: "Always slow. Never mean."

card end_close
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B ow_theory
title Close Enough
text Third sol. The drill bit snapped; the spare is in Cargo 2's hold, behind a door on ship power, and the rover's spare battery went to heaters. The ruling: spare power in hand. The drill says now. {A} counts the dark, nine, ten, eleven, and answers anyway. HELLO RX · OK. Its patch wakes heaters and door. The HOLD goes on the next tick. By then it has nothing left to hear it with. A galley screen blinks ONLINE, then OFFLINE. {B} puts a glove flat on the cold hull for eleven seconds. They drive home cold, the bit in {B}'s lap. To Starbase: "Landed. All eight. The ninth paid for the drill." From a loading bay: "It always did overpack."

